This is the kind of "designer fiat" that bothers me.  It introduces a
very obvious inconsistency -- ie. why does one type of fire hurt you,
but another type of fire doesn't?  (I already have an example of this
inconsistency in the game with the pyrolisk's and magical eye's gaze
elemental attacks -- even 100% resistance still provides half damage.
People haven't shrieked about that yet, but then again, people are
targeting the magical eyes for reasons far more important than being
plinked by fire/frost gaze, too, so it may be under everyone's radar.
I'm not very happy about even _that_ one being in, but it's an
experiment.)

